  "rhythm": "pianoletternotes columns: the intro arpeggio repeats every 32 columns and the melody's running notes are 2 columns, so 4 columns = one beat (running notes are eighths); long held notes kept at full length; last note cut to 1 beat to stay under the 20 s cap. Tempo 138 BPM from Hooktheory (songbpm agrees); 44 beats = 19.1 s | 2026-09-30 full-band remaster for Poodleskirt: VGMusic's m64docks.mid (130 BPM, quantized) plays the melody with exactly these notes and onsets (its answer phrase has the A3, like Hooktheory; diredock6.0.mid has D-G there instead, outvoted). The game adds layers as the level goes on; the MIDI's fuller loop (from its beat 404) is the source here: song beat 0 = its beat 452.5 (the pickup D), with its beats 444-452.5 as an 8.5-beat intro. Last note restored from 1 to 2 beats (its length in the MIDI), 45 beats = 19.6 s at 138 BPM (Hooktheory, songbpm). Band from that loop, all +2 like the melody: GM percussion (kick, snare, pedal-hat sixteenths), the fretless bass line, the vibraphone arpeggio with the melody notes removed (up to E4), and the string pads an octave down. General MIDI sound font for the vibraphone and fretless bass.",
